WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.762
Pre-aggregation can help control grain.

00:00:02.762 --> 00:00:06.852
First summarize the fact table to the level you actually need.

00:00:06.852 --> 00:00:10.787
Then perform later joins or pivots from that stable grain.

00:00:10.787 --> 00:00:17.672
This separates fact aggregation from presentation reshaping and can make the query easier to verify.

00:00:17.672 --> 00:00:22.167
Joining detail tables before reshaping can multiply rows.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:27.432
If the target is one row per patient or product, summarize each one-to-many source to the target grain

00:00:27.432 --> 00:00:29.957
before combining them.

00:00:29.957 --> 00:00:35.384
This keeps measures interpretable and prevents a pivot from hiding earlier join inflation.
